newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.unix.sys5.r4

Try to guess who I am (g3adley@cdf.toronto.edu) wrote:
:   I have a program which can be compiled in V.  However, when I compile it
: under OSF/1 using cc, I got several error messages that told me the following 
: files do not exist.

: /usr/include/sys/feature_tests.h
: /usr/include/sys/machtype.h
: /usr/include/sys/unistd.h
: /usr/include/sys/t_lock.h
: /usr/include/sys/machlock.h
: /usr/include/sys/dki_lkiinfo.h
: /usr/include/sys/dl.h
: /usr/include/sys/sleepq.h
: /usr/include/sys/turnstile.h
: /usr/include/sys/mutex.h
: /usr/include/sys/strmdep.h
: /usr/include/sys/byteorder.h
: /usr/include/vm/seg_enum.h

:   Could anyone tell me where these files are supposed to be in OSF/1?

Looks like you're porting a device driver or something that goes in the
kernel.  UNIX SVR4 supports what's called the DDI/DKI (Device Driver
Interface/Device Kernel Interface) that defines all of these interfaces
that a driver can use.  However, non SVR4 UNIX platforms (such as OSF/1)
do not support the same interfaces.  So, aside from the missing header
files, you will have siginificant porting work ahead of you to make your
code fit an OSF/1 kernel.

Sorry for the bad news.

-Ti
