In article <Pine.SOL.3.91.951130153702.25664A-100000@info.census.gov>,
"Joyce Cooper (EPCD)" <joycec@Census.GOV> wrote:

>  If I try going into these directories 
> to remove the files 'cd os!2_sys' e.g., I get the error message "2: event 
> not found".  
> 
>   Any suggestions? 
> 

Whenever referring to an object that contains an exclaimation point, try
quoting the symbol with a backslash.  I.e., try:

cd os\!2_sys

Same goes for rm and rmdir.  This quoting inhibits the shell from
interpreting the exclaimation point as a history event.



