>We have an FDDI loop that until 2 weeks ago consisting of... 


I worked in FDDI for seven years, i have designed SMT software, and 
futhermore a testing device for FDDI rings.
I hope to be able to give you some usefull informations.
LEM means Link Error Monitor, it is in fact an automate included
in SMT, which monitors the optical link quality (in fact it tries
to give an estimation of the Bit Error Rate).
The standard recommends to remove a connection with excessive LER
(Link Error Rate).
The LEM events identify  link errors events (like receiving noise,
when the ring is operationnal).
During a physical connection (monitors by PCM i.e Physical Connection 
Management), a link confidence test (LCT) is performed to check the link
quality. The values of parameters associated to LEM an LCT mean, i think
that a physical link (optical fiber, connector ...) or a tranceiver is not 
ok.
Therefore your network loses or corrupts frames (lost and error frames 
counters), and sometimes the token is lost, and a ring reconfiguration
occurs (e.g mac(s) initialisation using claim and beacon frames).
The origine of your problem can be either due to an electronic board, or
to a cable or connector default. 
