    You can't believe any of the estimates or feet remaining values ---
they are all veterans of the open-reel tape era.

>
>Assuming that the tape isn't full (it should be more than 4% full, but 
>not by much... the /extra disk has about 80Mb of stuff on it) how would I 
>go about doing a level 0 dump of the other partitions (/, /usr, /var) on 
>the same tape? 

    You would have to do all your dumps to the tape using the no-rewind tape
device, e.g. /dev/nrmt0h.
 
