s28454@nntpserver.sp.ac.sg (Dr Hu Yufan) writes:
>On a DEC Alpha/OSF1 system I am accessing, there are lots of files whose 
>names starting with '#.'. I remember I read somewhere that these files are 
>temporary files and can be removed without problem. Is that true?

If they both start and end with '#', they are probably emacs temporary files
used for journaling. They are created by emacs as a periodic save file during a
session and are deleted when the file is saved. If the editor does not save the
file before exiting, they live on until the file is next edited. Unless they
are yours or very old, I'd be careful about leaving them.

