|> I receive the following error when trying to invoke dxlsm while
|> running CDE:
|> 
|> 
|> #dxlsm
|> X Error of failed request:  BadFont (invalid Font parameter)
|>   Major opcode of failed request:  56 (X_ChangeGC)
|>   Resource id in failed request:  0xc01648f0
|>   Serial number of failed request:  7057
|>   Current serial number in output stream:  7645
|> 
|> 
|> Does anybody know how to fix this?
|> 
|> Thanx.
|> Marius.
|> 
|> 

CDE exposed an existing font handling problem in dxlsm. In the interim,
take a look at /usr/dt/config/C/sys.font. Extract the resource definition

*FontList: xxxx

from the file, remove the trailing ":" character, and add that entry
to your .Xdefaults file. dxlsm should behave the next time you log in.
Alternatively, you could edit the system version in /usr/dt/config/C/sys.font.
This will be fixed in the next major release of Digital UNIX.

Chris



