Hi all,

I've just spent about two hours tracking down a line of code that manages to
crash my X sessions completely, leaving huge core dump files in the root
directory. Its hard to know which process is actually biting the bullet first,
but most likely the Xdec X server, as it always falls over with a particular
call to the XParseColor() function. Its likely that my code isn't great,
however it really manages to bring the whole of X down, even through a
debugger. From all perspectives - its a BUG.

The next thing I did was to look through my documentation to find a bug report
address, but as you might guess with the quality of DEC's docs, I didn't manage
to find one. SO, I thought I would at least let the poor users know (you), and
also hope that someone from the OSF might read this, and send me a pointer to
report the thing.

Phil

