g3adley@cdf.toronto.edu wrote:

>  I have a program which can be compiled in V.  However, when I compile >  it under OSF/1 using cc, I got several error messages that told me 
>  the following files do not exist.
>
>/usr/include/sys/feature_tests.h
>/usr/include/sys/machtype.h
>/usr/include/sys/unistd.h
>/usr/include/sys/t_lock.h
>/usr/include/sys/machlock.h
>/usr/include/sys/dki_lkiinfo.h
>/usr/include/sys/dl.h
>/usr/include/sys/sleepq.h
>/usr/include/sys/turnstile.h
>/usr/include/sys/mutex.h
>/usr/include/sys/strmdep.h
>/usr/include/sys/byteorder.h
>/usr/include/vm/seg_enum.h
>
> Could anyone tell me where these files are supposed to be in OSF/1?

Only one of these files exists on Digital UNIX:
/usr/include/unistd.h

There is a file called "/usr/include/mach_types.h".  Perhaps this is the
same as "/usr/include/sys/machtype.h".

