references: <WALTER.95Nov27141533@hilbert.edv.agrar.tu-muenchen.de>
to: walter@pollux.edv.agrar.tu-muenchen.de (Bernhard Walter)
organization: Digital Equipment Corporation
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

>walter@pollux.edv.agrar.tu-muenchen.de (Bernhard Walter) writes:

>Since a few days I have an DEC AXPpci33 with "OSF1 hilbert V3.2 214 alpha" 
>(uname -a). I'm working with a 82 kHz monitor at the console, the machine
>has an ATI64 graphics adapter. It is configured for a size of 1024x768
>(as is also shown by '/usr/sbin/sizer -gr'), but both ATI64 and my monitor
>can display 1280x1024. I browsed some config files in /usr/lib/X11/xdm and
>/var/adm/X11, but I cannot find a way to configure the X-server for higher
>resolution. 

Edit /usr/lib/X11/xdm/Xservers and add "-screen 1280" to the end
of the ":0" line.  You should end up with something like:

:0 local /usr/bin/X11/X -screen 1280

