: instruction.  After this, I cannot even kill dbx: ps says it's an
: 'uninterruptable sleeping process'.  Any ideas, folks?

SIGTRAP is the mechanism used internally to do process tracing. The
"uninterruptability" is derived from the fact the it is being blocked
in a high-level system call. Are you using "sproc"? (I am unfamiliar 
with OSF.alpha -- sorry). On some systems, a program called "dbxhang"
is provided for just this contigency. This is probably not enough info;
but perhaps some dbx guru "out there" with deign to reply?

-Brian



