Mike,
  If you haven't gotten an answer yet (my news feed is 5-10 days late)
you can create a "default" entry in the /etc/gettydefs file like so :

default# B9600 #9600 #\r\nThis is a test.\r\nWill this print on line \
two?\r\nThis is number 3\r\n#

The other method is to replace the login program with a c program that
will display a message file and then exec the real login :


#include <stdio.h>
main(int argc, char **argv) {
        FILE *issue_f;
        char c;
        if((issue_f=fopen("/etc/issue","r"))!=NULL) {
                while((c=getc(issue_f))!=EOF)
                        putchar(c);
                fclose(issue_f);
        }
        execvp("/usr/lib/login.real",argv);
}


