Hi... I have a DEC 2000 alpha system running DigitalUNIX 3.2c, which is 
going to be used as a mail/web/ftp server for my high school within a few 
months... It will be kept in an area which most people wont have access 
to normally, but not locked or hidden.  Anyone feeling malicious could 
walk in and do whatever they want to it, but I'm more worried about the 
janitors bumping it...  For people unfamiliar with its case, it has a 
lock on the front, which according to the manual is "unused, ignore its 
position".  It also has a case lock on the back, which will be locked.  
On the front is also a nice "halt" button, which isn't easy to bump, but 
not really protected either... I dont want people to be able to trash our 
servers just by hitting a simple halt button, especially since I (or 
someone who knows what they are doing) might not get there to restart it 
for a day or two.

I was thinking about popping open the case and somehow disabling that 
button (I suppose they could still just flip the power switch, but I 
think that would be a lot more malicious, and if they are going to do 
that, they could just unplug the system too!) but I was wondering what 
would happen if for some reason I need to halt the system (if it crashes 
for example!)

Does anyone have any ideas on this?

Also, I'm still trying to figure out how to connect to a PPP account at 
my local ISP, so if anyone can help, that would be great!

Thanks,
Scott
