My friends in Digital's file systems group tell me that they are
working hard on fixing the bugs in AdvFS that have made it difficult
to use AdvFS for storing USENET articles.  They would like to hear
about as many bugs as possible (since they can't fix the bugs they
don't know about.)

As an experiment in gathering customer input, I volunteered to
solicit news-related AdvFS bug reports.  If you are using AdvFS
to store news articles, or tried but gave up, and have a bug to
report, send it to me via email.  I will collect the reports and
forward them to the file systems engineers.

Please make your reports as complete and as self-contained as possible.
Don't assume that the people reading them are experts on USENET.
And please include specific details such as software version numbers,
what kind of disks you're using, the approximate number of news
articles, etc.

They already know about these news-related bugs:
        Bitfile Metadata (BMT) extent exhaustion
        "bs_real_invalidate_pages: buf refd or pinned" panics
        "can't clear bits twice" panics
so there is no need to report them.

Also, if you have discovered any useful techniques for using
AdvFS with news, please let us know.  I'm trying to convince
them to include this sort of info in the documentation.

Thanks
-Jeff
mogul@pa.dec.com



