In order to use a new disk you must:
1) note on what SSCI port you connect it. If your machine
has two SCSI port the second port (B) address could be referred
by add 8 to the real address.
2) in /dev run ./MAKEDEV rz<address>
3) create the file system with newfs command for each partition
that you decide to use. If the disk is not known by your machine
you must add it on the /etc/disktab file, where you could
specified the partition name and size.
4) mount the disk. For automount at bootstrap see fstab file

I hope this can help you
Gianluca Mazzini



