tulachan@cco.caltech.edu (Pravin V. Tulachan) wrote:


>I have two questions:
>1) How does one set up virtual web host on DEC Alphastation 3000/500 running
>OSF/1 V2.1 lately called Digital UNIX? I would like to have couple of sites
>such as www.geodata.com, www.coresw.com and www.bigmachine.com all defaulting
>to one ip address but with separate web directores.

I am in the same boat sort of. Right now the Apache (it is public
domain...www.apache.org I believe) web server allows you to map
different URL/Domain names to one ethernet port.

You tell it that if a request comes in with www.geodata.com you give
it the default fie geo.index (or a file in another directory)

and if they come in with www.coresw.com it gives a different default
file.

The problem I have run into is that it is not just the Apache server
you need (BTW Netscape is working on implementing these features in
their new server version). You also need your OS to be able to handle
mapping multiple IP numbers to one ethernet device.

I have been given a patch to Irix for my SGIs and have investigated it
on the Alpha.

I have a machine (actually two ofthem) with this configuration from
uname -a 
OSF1 loki.atcon.com V3.2 214 alpha

If you do a man on ifconfig it tells you there is an alias option for
ifconfig.  the question I have is will this do more than 2 IPs? They
suggest the reason you use it is if you change your IP on the machine,
it is a way to have your ethernet respond to the old IP for a while in
case certain machines on the Net have not updated their DNSs.

If that is the case, it seems to be a primary-secondary system and
probably does not allow any more than one alias.

anyone used this with ifconfig before? Any help is appreciated.

DANO





