being a DEC device, the TZ87 is much better supported by the drivers.
Mine is dead stable so far, about a factor of 2 faster and the media will
last many,many head passes (some I'v e read and read and read over 100 times 
now, no trouble...) Only drawback: once you wrote a new header on a DLT, there 
is NO WAY to read all the remaining data behind this (due to a firmware "feature")

My exa8505s does see only two uses since I've the TZ87:
read data off previously recorded 8mm (just once!) to copy it to TZ87
and to write 8mm tapes for some external group members who are still stuck 
with these. Reliablity was always a real trouble with 8mm, both media and drives.

I did not have any trouble with TZ87 (=DLT2000) so far.

Uwe



