From: Angela Bao <bao>
Subject: keymapping for Vt100 emulation
Date: 1995/11/14
Message-ID: <1995Nov14.145454.171@bbs.ug.eds.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 119439291
content-type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
x-url: news:comp.unix.osf.osf1
mime-version: 1.0
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1
x-mailer: Mozilla 1.1N (X11; I; HP-UX A.09.05 9000/710)

Hello OSFers,

  Several weeks ago I asked the net for help defining the keypad to 
emulate vt100, used to telnet to a VMS box.  No one helped me.
Digital support wasn't helpful either.  So I came up with my own solution.
All you need to do is add the following lines to
/usr/lib/X11/app-defaults/XTerm, invoke an xterm named VMSTERM, 
e.g.   xterm -name VMSTERM

This redefines the function keys F1-F4 as the PF1-PF4 keys, 
also, PF1 = F1 (the GOLD key)
      PF2 = F2 = /
      PF3 = F3 = *
      PF4 = F4 = -

The key redefinition is only active in that specific "xterm", 
so it doesn't affect any other dtterm or applications.
Hopefully someone will find it useful someday.

XTerm*VT100.Translations:   #override Meta<KeyPress>: insert-seven-bit()
VMSTERM*VT100.Translations: #override \n\
 <Key>F1:               string(0x1b) string(OP)\n\
 <Key>F2:               string(0x1b) string(OQ)\n\
 <Key>F3:               string(0x1b) string(OR)\n\
 <Key>F4:               string(0x1b) string(OS)\n\
 <Key>KP_Divide:        string(0x1b) string(OQ)\n\
 <Key>KP_Multiply:      string(0x1b) string(OR)\n\
 <Key>KP_Subtract:      string(0x1b) string(OS)\n\
 <Key>KP_Add:           string(0x1b) string(Om)\n\
 <Key>KP_Enter:         string(0x1b) string(OM)\n\
 <Key>KP_0:             string(0x1b) string(Op)\n\
 <Key>KP_1:             string(0x1b) string(Oq)\n\
 <Key>KP_2:             string(0x1b) string(Or)\n\
 <Key>KP_3:             string(0x1b) string(Os)\n\
 <Key>KP_4:             string(0x1b) string(Ot)\n\
 <Key>KP_5:             string(0x1b) string(Ou)\n\
 <Key>KP_6:             string(0x1b) string(Ov)\n\
 <Key>KP_7:             string(0x1b) string(Ow)\n\
 <Key>KP_8:             string(0x1b) string(Ox)\n\
 <Key>KP_9:             string(0x1b) string(Oy)\n\
 <Key>KP_Decimal:       string(0x1b) string(On)\n\
 <Key>BackSpace:        string(0x7f)


enjoy,
angela
