Hey Chris,

Two things have to be done.

1. reconfigure the kernel to include the drive. I you are unsure how, do the
   following.

a. shutdown to boot prompt:
b. boot the standard kernel
	boot -fl s -file genvmunix
c. when booted run the sizer command
	sizer -n newconfig
   "sizer" will create /tmp/newconfig and /tmp/newconfig.devs where the first is
   a config file with the new device in it and the second is a script to do the
   MAKEDEV's.
d. include the differences in the device section of /tmp/newconfig into 
   /sys/conf/<local kernel name>.
e. rebuild kernel
   doconfig -c /sys/conf/<kernel name>
f. move new kernel "/sys/<kernel name>/vmunix to / and run /tmp/newconfig.devs
g. reboot multi

This should do it.

Cheers,

John

