Our alpha running DEC OSF/1 V3.2 is experiencing a problem with processes
not going away after the user terminates his session.  By terminate I mean
aborting a telnet session, which should normally send a hangup (SIGHUP) to
all processes connected to the users tty port.  The hangup signal never
gets sent, leaving numerous processes still running which have to be killed
off with a special killer script.  This was verified by manually sending a
hangup with "kill -HUP proc_ID", in which case the process promptly dies.

On our DEC ULTRIX machine this problem does not occur, even though the
exact same type of session aborting occurs.

I checked the gettydefs file and all lines have the HUPCL flag as required.

Has anyone had a similar experience with hung processes, and if so, what did
you do to fix it?  Any comments/suggestions would be greatly appreciated.

