Hello,

Recently, a new addition has been made to the Alphaserver WWW and ftp
area.  The firmware for *all* Alpha platforms (servers and
workstations) is now available for download.  These additions have
been made in conjunction with the folks who create the official
firmware CD, and will continue to be updated as new versions of the CD
are released.  In addition, when any Alpha platform releases a new
version of their firmware between CD releases, it will be made
available in an interim directory.

The location of the files are as follows:

Via ftp:
	ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Alpha/firmware/

Via WWW:
	http://www.service.digital.com/alpha/server/firmware/

The files are structured similiar to those on the firmware CD, and are
separated by CD release.  For example, the contents of the V3.3
firmware CD are located at: 
	ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Alpha/firmware/v3.3/

The latest and greatest firmware (if released since the last firmware
CD) is located at:
	ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Alpha/firmware/interim/


We hope that these pages will be useful.  Please send your comments and
feedback to alpha_server@service.digital.com

FAQ maintainers are encouraged to add this resource to their lists.


enjoy,

