I recently did this on a DEC OSF/1 3.0.  The command is:

ifconfig tu0 alias <IP Address>

With this feature, you set up another IP address for the ethernet card.  DEC
says the limit is approx 250 addresses.  

Then go into your webserver configuration and tell one server to bind to one IP
address and the other to bind to another IP address.  

Oh DEC warns that bootp will probably not work after this.  If your using
bootp, it's not recommended that you run multiple IPs.

Bill




