You should be able to buy a 2100 without a monitor, but they all come
with a 1280x1024 EISA video card.  What we did was put a cheap $300
VGA monitor on our 2100 and it works fine.

Rainer> Question: is it possible to run a 2100 without video card, and 
Rainer> attach, say, a vt100 to a serial port as a console (as it was
Rainer> possible with the TurboChannel machines)?

Yes, according to the systems and options catalog you should be able
to do all work on a serial console. 

Rainer> And the same question about the Server 2000

It too comes with a graphics card (1024x768) but you can do all ECU
and RCU functions while using a serial console.

Rainer> Other questions: What is the recommended minimal memory
Rainer> configuration and how many CPUs are at least needed, to use
Rainer> the machine as a file server for, say, 10 workstations, using
Rainer> a RAID disk array of 5*4GB?

It depends on how active this system will be.  If all it will be doing
is NFS service, with no logins, then 64Mb should be fine.  If you
expect to have people logged in at the same time doing stuff, then I'd
recommend more memory.  You'll only need 1 CPU for this system.

If all you're going to be doing with this system is NFS service, you
might want to think of getting one of the cheaper, smaller systems
with an external storageworks shelf.  But it all really depends on how
much expandability you want with the system.

