One simple thing you can do with the system is shut it down
gracefully, put on a anti-static strap, open it up and blow out the
dust, reseat all the boards, make sure the cables are snug, close it
up and reboot.

If you keep getting machine check crashes, then it's time to call DEC
and have their people look at the crash info and decide if it's a
motherboard, disk or CPU module problem.  Or memory, though normally
you would get memory error message if your memory was going bad.

