>>>>> "OB" == Oleg Bartunov <megera@sai.msu.su> writes:
In article <slrn49poq2.h6g.megera@ra.sai.msu.su> megera@sai.msu.su (Oleg Bartunov) writes:


OB> Hi, I need utility like ldd in Solaris to extract names of libraries
OB> referenced from executable module. Actually, I want to setup
OB> anonymous ftp (wu-ftpd) under OSF 3.2 and need to know what
OB> libraries I have to copy to ~ftp/usr/lib directory. I copied
OB> /sbin/ls but it doesn't work. I think /sbin/ls also dynamically
OB> linked.

OB> 	Regards, Oleg

Oleg,

I think that you will find that /sbin/ls is actually statically linked
(as are all commands in the /sbin directory).  The command 

	odump -Dl /sbin/ls

will list all of the dynamic libraries used by the executable (none, in
this case).

I suspect that your real problem is that you haven't created an
~ftp/etc/sia directory containing the correct files.  If you look near
the end of the ftpd(8) manpage that comes with 3.2, you will find a
description of the directories and files required for the correct
operation of (any) ftpd.  (Even though this manpage suggests that
~ftp/etc/sia is optional, I am virtually positive that it is mandatory.)
You can create ~ftp/etc/sia by copying /etc/sia.

I hope that this helps!


Regards,
Neil

