From: lionel@quark.enet.dec.com (Steve Lionel)
Subject: DEC Fortran 90 Price Reduction, Combined Packaging with DEC Fortran
Date: 1995/11/07
Message-ID: <47oj89$ohp@zk2nws.zko.dec.com>
X-Deja-AN: 118855811
distribution: world
followup-to: poster
organization: Digital Equipment Corporation, Nashua NH
reply-to: lionel@quark.enet.dec.com (Steve Lionel)
newsgroups: comp.lang.fortran,comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.os.vms,comp.sys.dec


HIGHLIGHTS

*  DEC Fortran 90 concurrent license prices are being lowered by 14%,
   capacity prices are being lowered by an average of 10% on November 13,
   1995

*  The Fortran product line name on Alpha systems will change to 
   "Digital Fortran" in April 1996

*  The DEC Fortran (extended Fortran 77) compiler will continue to be 
   available on the new Digital Fortran kit


PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

For over 30 years, Digital has led the industry in supplying the most
technologically advanced, feature-rich Fortran compilers.  In more recent
history, Digital was one of the first to embrace the current ISO and ANSI
Fortran 90 standard on 64-bit systems with our DEC Fortran 90 product.  On
Digital UNIX, Digital became the first vendor to include support for the
complete High Performance Fortran (HPF) Specification, which allows
customers to write and execute parallel HPF programs.  In May 1995, Digital
expanded this premier family of compilers with support for OpenVMS Alpha.

The Fortran 90 language is a superset of Fortran 77, so no "conversion" to
Fortran 90 is required.  Furthermore, since DEC Fortran 90 supports nearly all
DEC Fortran extensions, most Fortran users can switch to DEC Fortran 90 with
no source changes needed and no loss of performance.  Programmers can then
begin to explore the rich features of the Fortran 90 language and HPF (on
Digital UNIX) at their own pace in order to improve application performance,
take advantage of new architectures, and improve program maintainability.

The Gartner Group recently reviewed the major Fortran 90 compilers running
on UNIX operating systems to determine which vendors and technologies will
be the worldwide HPC leaders in the late 1990's.  The results placed Digital
at the top of the twelve leading systems and software vendors supplying
Fortran.  "Bottom Line: It is clear that the strongest language strategy is
Digital Equipment's because it provides support for both Fortran 90 and HPF
as well as a parallel debugger and multiple levels of optimization."
(Gartner Group, HPC Research Note, KA-220-329, July 1995).

Now, Digital wants to make it easier for customers to use DEC Fortran 90.  On
November 13, 1995 the prices for DEC Fortran 90 will be decreased. In April
1996, the following important changes will occur in the DEC Fortran and DEC
Fortran 90 product lines. 

*  DEC Fortran 90 and DEC Fortran will be consolidated into one kit and
   renamed "Digital Fortran".  The next version, Digital Fortran V4.0 on
   Digital UNIX and V7.0 on OpenVMS Alpha, will be released in April 1996.

*  The products and license PAKs will be engineered so that customers with
   current DEC Fortran or DEC Fortran 90 PAKs can run either product if they
   upgrade to the new release in April.  This protects our customers' 
   investment in Fortran from Digital.

*  Service customers for both DEC Fortran and DEC Fortran 90 will receive the
   new Digital Fortran release at no charge.  Other customers may purchase
   an update license.

*  DEC Fortran for OpenVMS VAX, an extended Fortran 77 product, is not
   affected by this change.  A maintenance release, V6.4, is scheduled for
   March 1996.

SERVICES

A complete range of software support, update, and license subscription
services is available worldwide. Users can purchase Telephone Support
Service, New Version License Subscription Service, a Packaged Service that
provides the rights to use new versions and updates to the software, and the
Documentation Update Distribution Service.  When the two Fortrans are
combined in April 1996, customers with valid contracts for either DEC
Fortran or DEC Fortran 90 will be covered for both products.


RESOURCES

*  Web Page (URL http://www.digital.com/info/hpc/f90/)
*  "Fortran from Digital" product brief (EC-F5383-93 - send mail to
   fortran90@digital.com to request a copy)
*  Gartner Group states Digital has the strongest Fortran language strategy
   of the twelve top Fortran providers worldwide (send mail to
   fortran90@digital.com to request a copy)
*  E-mail to product managers (fortran90@digital.com)
*  Digital Technical Journal article on DEC Fortran 90 & PSE
   (Coming in December 1995 - send mail to fortran90@digital.com for more
   information.)

