19.29 builds on the alpha out of the box. There is no longer a need to patch
things.

But, if you are looking for a reasonable emacs for a Motif environment, I'd
strongly suggest that you look at XEmacs
(ftp.cs.uiuc.edu:/pub/exmacs/xemacs-19.13.tar.gz)
It's also available as pre-compiled binaries and libs, although I have never
tried using the Digital UNIX version, (The SunOS one works for me, though.)

XEmacs has a MUCH nicer X interface including Motif-like scroll bars and
pull-down menus and a tool-bar for the more common functions. Since they
actually use the Lucid toolkit, you don't even need Motif, but that's hardly an
issue for most Digital UNIX systems. (Don't try to use the Motif menus and
scroll-bars unless you want a very slow editor.)

It is virtually identical to emacs from the user perspective, although the
elisp programmer may need to do a little fixing up, especially if using the X
interface tools. (These are totally different from emacs19.) It took me about
an hour to convert one rather large module that does pop-up menus and the like.

