: system PRIVILEGED account (root@decosf1.dbf.ddb.de) wrote:
: : Hi there,

: : is there a way to display some information BEFORE the user logs in?
: : In Linux it is /etc/issue which I can use to display some info. Is
: : there something like that in DUNIX 3.2c ???

What we have done in the past is to replace the login program with:

#include <stdio.h>
main(int argc, char **argv) {
	FILE *issue_f;
	char c;
	if((issue_f=fopen("/etc/issue","r"))!=NULL) {
		while((c=getc(issue_f))!=EOF)
			putchar(c);
		fclose(issue_f);
	}
	execvp("/usr/lib/login.real",argv);
}

Note, you should copy the Digital supplied login to /usr/lib/login.real
and you might need to redo the changes after an operating system update.
