|>c-shell script, but assign doesn't appear to be available on the alpha.
|>
|>How do I read a big endian and write a little endian unformatted file?
|>I have been working with in FORTRAN, so that solution would be prefered.
|>I know a little C, so if someone could tell me the pertinent statements,
|>I could probably muddle my way through!  ;)

There are three DEC Fortran "hammers" with which you can affect the 
data-conversion attribute of I/O.  You've picked the biggest one, the
compile command switch, which affects all I/O on all units.  The next smaller
hammer is to define an environment variable of the form FORT_CONVERTn, where
"n" is the unit number, before running the program.  The value of the variable
is the convert type wanted for that unit, for example, BIG_ENDIAN.  The
smallest hammer is the CONVERT= keyword on the OPEN statement for the
file you want to use.

For more information, please read the chapter on non-native data conversion
during I/O in the DEC Fortran User Manual.
