With <Pine.SOL.3.91.951031151447.18121A-100000@count51.med.harvard.edu>,
it seems Matthew Weed (mweed@count51.med.harvard.edu) sez:

+ I have just been given a station running DEC UNIX(3.2 I believe), and 
+ other than pine, which I have successfully compiled to that machine, I 
+ have had trouble finding other newsreaders/posting agents that will work 
+ on that machine.  I am quite particular to trn, but am willing to learn 
+ new readers should this prove necessary.  if anyone can point me in the 
+ direction of newsreaders (and in the case of trn, inews as well), that 
+ will work under v3.2, i would appreciate it.
+ If possible, please send the ftp site, and any directory  information 
+ necessary to complete the transfer.

I suggest tin.  Version 1.22 is the last stable release, and version
1.3 is well along in the beta testing.  It presents a pseudo-menu
based interface which allows movement between threads, articles,
newsgroups, etc, much easier (IMHO) than [t]rn.  It supports NNTP,
Overview files, comes with a builtin inews, etc, etc.

You can get it from ftp://ftp.scn.de/pub/news/clients/tin .

